1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,570
(All people, organizations, businesses,
events, and places shown are fictional.)

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,005
(Child actors filmed in a safe space
with their guardians present.)

3
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,179
What brings you here?

4
00:00:12,546 --> 00:00:15,148
I'm giving you now what I couldn't
give you then.

5
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:16,383
Author Kkong Kkong.

6
00:00:17,518 --> 00:00:24,124
(Youth Recommended Book Award Ceremony)

7
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:25,859
(Congratulations to Author Kkong Kkong
on winning the grand prize.)

8
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:32,633
Author Kkong Kkong,
congratulations on the grand prize.

9
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:36,303
Found you, Oriole.

10
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:43,777
- So you were Mumu after all.
- You knew?

11
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:48,348
Not long ago, it suddenly occurred
to me that it might be you.

12
00:00:48,815 --> 00:00:50,017
So why didn't you tell me?

13
00:00:51,051 --> 00:00:52,586
I could've been wrong,

14
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:56,056
but I was actually hoping
you wouldn't find out.

15
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:57,558
Why not?

16
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:01,395
Why didn't you go to the ceremony?

17
00:01:02,329 --> 00:01:03,597
I waited for so long.

18
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:12,072
What? What is going on between you two?

19
00:01:14,041 --> 00:01:17,411
- I said, what's going on?
- Why are you coming out of there?

20
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:20,447
What's weirder than me being here...

21
00:01:20,681 --> 00:01:23,483
is "Oriole," "Mumu," and these flowers.

22
00:01:32,826 --> 00:01:34,828
What a twist of fate…

23
00:01:35,889 --> 00:01:36,978
It's well written.

24
00:01:37,831 --> 00:01:39,386
How can you tell by flipping through it?

25
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:40,811
Try reading it.

26
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:43,670
Reading scripts
is more than enough for me.

27
00:01:44,505 --> 00:01:45,466
You're right.

28
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:46,540
It's not a fun read.

29
00:01:46,907 --> 00:01:48,195
What are you talking about?

30
00:01:48,219 --> 00:01:49,420
Why would you say that?

31
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:51,411
Only you would think it's fun.

32
00:01:52,012 --> 00:01:53,547
Not everyone has to like it.

33
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:54,781
No, Yu Il.

34
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:56,814
If Mu I likes it, I like it too.

35
00:01:56,839 --> 00:01:58,118
Even though I've never read it.

36
00:01:59,753 --> 00:02:01,388
All right, thank you.

37
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:05,225
Well, the bouquet presentation is over,

38
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:07,728
and the fan meet seems about done too.

39
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:09,596
So let's go, Mu I.

40
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:14,110
Yu Il had a lot happen to her today.

41
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,536
If you care as a fan, let her rest.

42
00:02:24,745 --> 00:02:26,980
Yu Il's ex-boyfriend came by earlier.

43
00:02:27,414 --> 00:02:30,250
He had a thing with someone else,
pretty much ghosted Yu Il,

44
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:32,619
and now that his fling is over,
he wants her back.

45
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,756
He said her situation is worse
than his, so he'd do her a favor.

46
00:02:37,257 --> 00:02:39,760
What was his name?

47
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:42,062
Yong Seok. Kim Yong Seok, right?

48
00:02:42,462 --> 00:02:44,177
I don't know his name.

49
00:02:44,201 --> 00:02:45,432
How do you know?

50
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,002
I heard Yeon Ju speaking harshly of him.

51
00:02:50,404 --> 00:02:52,940
- He's total trash.
- Right?

52
00:02:53,807 --> 00:02:56,410
What do you think about people
getting back with their exes?

53
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:57,945
It never works out.

54
00:02:57,945 --> 00:02:59,780
Why restore a cracked mirror with glue?

55
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:03,417
It's ugly and uncomfortable to look at,
and it keeps falling apart.

56
00:03:03,617 --> 00:03:04,518
Right?

57
00:03:05,586 --> 00:03:06,553
By the way,

58
00:03:08,155 --> 00:03:09,590
are you not getting your license?

59
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:12,092
Nope, I'm never getting one.

60
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:14,695
That way, I can ride in your car forever.

61
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:21,101
(Community Board)

62
00:03:21,902 --> 00:03:23,670
It was so hard for me to find this.

63
00:03:23,694 --> 00:03:25,806
Has this online fan page been shut down?

64
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,041
(Community Board!)

65
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,152
Hey, about "Star and the Half Moon,"

66
00:03:30,177 --> 00:03:31,678
I really enjoyed reading it.

67
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:37,217
Knock, knock!
Hey, author, when can we read Book 3?

68
00:03:38,785 --> 00:03:39,686
(Community Board!)

69
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:42,623
I can't find you, Oriole.

70
00:03:55,903 --> 00:03:58,739
I'm glad that I can be "Mumu" again.

71
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:07,281
I'm also glad to meet Mumu again.

72
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:14,221
No, I'm saying don't get involved at all.

73
00:04:17,658 --> 00:04:19,493
(I'm also glad to meet Mumu…)

74
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:28,769
- Baby, did you enjoy the meal?
- Yeah, I'm so full.

75
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:30,671
- You're full? Me too.
- Yeah.

76
00:04:30,771 --> 00:04:33,240
- What should we do later?
- Are you going home tonight?

77
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,775
Home? Should I go or not?

78
00:04:34,975 --> 00:04:37,744
- May I clear your finished plates?
- Don't go, obviously.

79
00:04:37,945 --> 00:04:40,747
- Then, of course I won't go.
- Excuse me.

80
00:04:40,747 --> 00:04:42,850
I really love it too.
Let's come here again.

81
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:44,818
- Okay.
- Yeah, let's come every single day.

82
00:04:44,885 --> 00:04:46,220
- Do I look pretty?
- You look so pretty.

83
00:04:48,222 --> 00:04:49,389
- What on earth?
- Are you okay?

84
00:04:50,098 --> 00:04:52,301
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.

85
00:04:52,326 --> 00:04:55,095
This is so annoying.
Today is such an important day!

86
00:04:55,095 --> 00:04:58,198
I'm so sorry. Did I startle you?

87
00:04:58,198 --> 00:04:59,433
Your clothes? It didn't splash, right?

88
00:04:59,867 --> 00:05:01,535
The wine didn't splash,

89
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:03,403
but I'm so upset.

90
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:06,073
I'll bring new wine and food…

91
00:05:06,073 --> 00:05:07,508
That's not the issue.

92
00:05:07,508 --> 00:05:09,443
The wine glass just broke!

93
00:05:10,177 --> 00:05:11,778
The glass, not the wine?

94
00:05:11,912 --> 00:05:13,113
Is that really the issue right now?

95
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,582
How can you ruin our anniversary?

96
00:05:16,583 --> 00:05:18,752
It's bad luck on such a meaningful day.

97
00:05:18,752 --> 00:05:19,753
I know, right?

98
00:05:19,786 --> 00:05:21,822
If this is the reason my man and I
break up,

99
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,490
are you going to take responsibility?

100
00:05:25,092 --> 00:05:27,861
Miss Ye Ji, I'm the owner-chef,
Kang Hee Su.

101
00:05:27,861 --> 00:05:28,762
So?

102
00:05:30,998 --> 00:05:35,636
I do apologize about this,
and to celebrate your anniversary,

103
00:05:37,204 --> 00:05:39,840
I'd like to give you the wine
you were considering earlier.

104
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:43,677
- Would that be all right?
- Really? That's the super expensive one…

105
00:05:45,812 --> 00:05:46,847
Well…

106
00:05:47,814 --> 00:05:49,149
If you insist…

107
00:05:50,284 --> 00:05:51,251
Thank you.

108
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:56,757
Let us clean up the mess first.
Yu Il, if you could…

109
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:08,268
(Mom)

110
00:06:19,546 --> 00:06:20,714
(You're my only child…)

111
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,416
Yu Il, please get back to me.

112
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:25,285
Will you avoid your dad
for the rest of your life?

113
00:06:26,019 --> 00:06:27,821
You're my only child.

114
00:06:34,061 --> 00:06:35,028
Are you okay?

115
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:41,335
It's broken. Sorry about that.

116
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:43,704
It was already broken.

117
00:06:47,875 --> 00:06:50,611
Sorry about earlier… I mean, thank you…

118
00:06:55,182 --> 00:06:56,448
I'm sorry and grateful.

119
00:06:57,351 --> 00:06:58,986
About the cost of the wine…

120
00:06:59,052 --> 00:07:01,088
What happened to the outspoken part-timer

121
00:07:01,088 --> 00:07:03,357
who was so tough
with high school girls at the store?

122
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:05,492
You seem like a totally different person.

123
00:07:07,461 --> 00:07:10,330
I know. It makes me seem two-faced,
doesn't it?

124
00:07:10,831 --> 00:07:14,568
In front of a $1.50 popsicle,
I had no fear,

125
00:07:15,102 --> 00:07:17,471
but when I spilled a $250 bottle of wine,

126
00:07:17,804 --> 00:07:19,606
my vision suddenly became a blur,

127
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,375
and I couldn't speak…

128
00:07:25,179 --> 00:07:28,282
If something like that happens again,

129
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,050
think about what's in front of you.

130
00:07:30,551 --> 00:07:32,052
If you knocked over the wine,

131
00:07:32,219 --> 00:07:34,254
you only need to apologize for that.

132
00:07:34,655 --> 00:07:36,790
Whether the mistake is a $1.50 item…

133
00:07:37,157 --> 00:07:38,659
or a $250 one,

134
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:41,495
deciding what to do
and taking responsibility…

135
00:07:42,896 --> 00:07:44,598
is entirely my job as the owner.

136
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:49,603
What is it?

137
00:07:50,704 --> 00:07:53,340
I've worked all kinds of part-time jobs,

138
00:07:53,574 --> 00:07:56,977
but I've never worked for an owner
who spoke to a part-timer that way.

139
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:02,149
This is my first time saying it too.

140
00:08:06,987 --> 00:08:09,223
I've never had a part-timer like you.

141
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:13,227
Everyone assumes the owner
will handle it, or so I've heard.

142
00:08:17,297 --> 00:08:19,600
Thanks again for looking out.

143
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:23,670
You say "thank you" quite often.
It's cute.

144
00:08:24,997 --> 00:08:29,076
It makes me want to give you
a lot more reasons to be thankful.

145
00:08:38,252 --> 00:08:39,520
So tired.

146
00:08:57,004 --> 00:08:58,839
Another brutal day.

147
00:09:00,741 --> 00:09:02,176
So tired.

148
00:09:09,583 --> 00:09:10,584
Hey.

149
00:09:10,918 --> 00:09:12,686
Kkong, are you done with work?

150
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,321
Yeah, I just got home.

151
00:09:15,622 --> 00:09:18,125
My dear Kkong, was it another tough day?

152
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:19,826
Of course I'm tired.

153
00:09:19,826 --> 00:09:23,330
Hey, my arms, legs, shoulders,
and knees all ache.

154
00:09:25,866 --> 00:09:28,969
It must be so difficult
carrying all those dishes.

155
00:09:29,203 --> 00:09:31,972
If only you could earn money
by sitting down all day,

156
00:09:32,039 --> 00:09:33,874
wouldn't that be nice?

157
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,845
As if that would ever happen.

158
00:09:45,853 --> 00:09:46,920
Are you good at this?

159
00:09:47,521 --> 00:09:49,256
I can play all night on 50 cents.

160
00:09:49,723 --> 00:09:53,126
When I was 12, I just wouldn't come home,
so my mom…

161
00:09:56,296 --> 00:09:57,431
Cut!

162
00:09:57,965 --> 00:10:00,934
Rooftop Girl, you ruined the take
by clearing that round.

163
00:10:01,735 --> 00:10:03,203
So that's not allowed.

164
00:10:03,337 --> 00:10:05,606
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

165
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,274
Okay, let's go again!

166
00:10:07,741 --> 00:10:09,243
It's okay, Yu Il.

167
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:11,712
Sorry, it's my fault.

168
00:10:13,881 --> 00:10:14,848
Ready.

169
00:10:15,382 --> 00:10:16,383
Action!

170
00:10:17,451 --> 00:10:18,418
Are you good at this?

171
00:10:19,086 --> 00:10:20,787
I can play all night on 50 cents.

172
00:10:21,255 --> 00:10:22,523
When I was 12,

173
00:10:22,890 --> 00:10:25,292
I just wouldn't come home,
so my mom…

174
00:10:27,561 --> 00:10:28,529
Cut!

175
00:10:29,696 --> 00:10:30,831
Hey, this isn't working.

176
00:10:31,198 --> 00:10:33,233
Let's mute the arcade sound
and add it later.

177
00:10:33,534 --> 00:10:34,501
Okay.

178
00:10:34,635 --> 00:10:36,803
We'll shoot the reverse angle
from the next line!

179
00:10:38,605 --> 00:10:40,941
Yu Il, you're so awesome.

180
00:10:42,309 --> 00:10:44,978
- Sorry.
- You're so competitive.

181
00:10:46,113 --> 00:10:47,214
Hey!

182
00:10:47,481 --> 00:10:49,383
Can't you go easy on the game?

183
00:10:49,883 --> 00:10:50,851
No, it's fine.

184
00:10:50,851 --> 00:10:52,553
We're shooting the reverse now,

185
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:53,754
so only the actors will be on screen.

186
00:10:54,054 --> 00:10:55,689
So only your profile will show.

187
00:10:55,689 --> 00:10:57,524
You can do anything you want now.

188
00:10:57,724 --> 00:10:59,893
Just don't kill the other guy.

189
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:01,295
Keep the game going.

190
00:11:02,663 --> 00:11:04,598
Wait, can I just go home?

191
00:11:04,631 --> 00:11:05,699
No!

192
00:11:05,699 --> 00:11:08,001
Where can I find an extra on short notice?

193
00:11:08,702 --> 00:11:11,638
Sorry. We're shooting
this impromptu scene on the fly.

194
00:11:12,539 --> 00:11:14,675
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

195
00:11:14,775 --> 00:11:16,310
I don't belong here anyway…

196
00:11:19,046 --> 00:11:20,047
Director!

197
00:11:20,547 --> 00:11:22,082
Can we take a short break?

198
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,685
I need to use the restroom.

199
00:11:38,665 --> 00:11:39,700
It's fine.

200
00:11:40,634 --> 00:11:41,635
It went smoothly.

201
00:11:43,437 --> 00:11:46,139
I couldn't be more of a nuisance.

202
00:11:47,007 --> 00:11:50,811
Sure, it's near my house
and they're paying me $100.

203
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,679
But I shouldn't have come at all.

204
00:11:54,081 --> 00:11:56,083
I had a really stressful day today,

205
00:11:56,483 --> 00:11:58,552
so I think I was taking it out
on that game.

206
00:12:00,053 --> 00:12:03,023
Still, I'm glad I get to see you
in person, Author Kkong.

207
00:12:04,124 --> 00:12:06,059
Please don't call me that.

208
00:12:06,326 --> 00:12:09,029
But you are Author Kkong.
What else should I call you?

209
00:12:10,964 --> 00:12:13,901
I'm too sleepy to even fight right now.

210
00:12:16,770 --> 00:12:17,771
Hold on.

211
00:12:23,443 --> 00:12:24,678
Hey, you should've asked me!

212
00:12:25,412 --> 00:12:27,181
No, I wanted to choose them myself.

213
00:12:28,148 --> 00:12:30,851
Lately, you've been doing a lot
of things you never do.

214
00:12:31,685 --> 00:12:32,719
- Yeong Su.
- Yeah?

215
00:12:32,819 --> 00:12:33,820
Is my hair okay?

216
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:36,823
- How was my acting today?
- What's going on here?

217
00:12:37,357 --> 00:12:40,060
You're asking things you never ask.
This is suspicious.

218
00:12:41,328 --> 00:12:43,197
That'll be $148.

219
00:12:44,531 --> 00:12:45,933
No, no, put it on mine.

220
00:12:45,933 --> 00:12:47,367
No, we can get reimbursement.

221
00:12:47,534 --> 00:12:49,536
I want to buy these myself.

222
00:12:50,504 --> 00:12:53,006
Excuse me, a signature, please.

223
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,542
Sorry, we're in a hurry right now.

224
00:12:55,876 --> 00:12:56,844
Pardon?

225
00:12:57,110 --> 00:13:00,647
No, not that kind. I'm asking you
to sign on the card terminal.

226
00:13:00,781 --> 00:13:02,916
For purchases over $100, you have to sign.

227
00:13:06,386 --> 00:13:09,056
The signature for the purchase.
Of course I should sign.

228
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:12,059
Thank you. Do you need a receipt?

229
00:13:12,192 --> 00:13:13,227
One for you.

230
00:13:13,227 --> 00:13:14,328
Thank you.

231
00:13:15,162 --> 00:13:16,230
Here you go.

232
00:13:19,199 --> 00:13:20,501
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

233
00:13:20,501 --> 00:13:21,535
Thank you so much.

234
00:13:27,574 --> 00:13:28,709
Hey, thank you.

235
00:13:29,409 --> 00:13:31,478
Wait, you don't drink coffee at night.

236
00:13:31,778 --> 00:13:34,047
A night like this calls for it,
for the shoot later.

237
00:13:34,848 --> 00:13:37,584
- You have more to shoot?
- Yeah, an outdoor street scene.

238
00:13:37,918 --> 00:13:39,753
Looks like I'll be working until dawn.

239
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:41,255
I'm already tired.

240
00:13:41,889 --> 00:13:44,391
- Yu Il, can I drink this?
- Sure.

241
00:13:44,391 --> 00:13:45,893
Thank you. I need the restroom.

242
00:13:48,095 --> 00:13:49,696
You seemed tired. That was for you.

243
00:13:51,265 --> 00:13:52,766
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

244
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:00,674
He gave all of them out, too.

245
00:14:01,775 --> 00:14:04,411
I'm really fine. I'm wide awake.

246
00:14:05,546 --> 00:14:07,314
Okay, let's bring it back, everyone!

247
00:14:08,015 --> 00:14:08,982
Okay.

248
00:14:11,151 --> 00:14:12,152
Are you good at this?

249
00:14:12,619 --> 00:14:14,121
I can play all night on 50 cents.

250
00:14:14,655 --> 00:14:15,661
When I was 12,

251
00:14:16,274 --> 00:14:20,160
I just wouldn't come home, so my mom
found me in the arcade the next morning.

252
00:14:20,794 --> 00:14:23,630
So I told her I'd waste money
if I didn't finish that round.

253
00:14:23,864 --> 00:14:24,998
Cut. Cut!

254
00:14:25,532 --> 00:14:26,834
So frustrating.

255
00:14:27,501 --> 00:14:29,870
- Hey, Rooftop Girl!
- Yes?

256
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:31,972
You keep looking at the camera!

257
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:35,175
You know what? You can go now.

258
00:14:36,176 --> 00:14:37,144
Pardon?

259
00:14:37,144 --> 00:14:39,213
I said you can go. You're done.

260
00:14:40,581 --> 00:14:41,615
Okay.

261
00:14:42,115 --> 00:14:43,784
Where's So Na, the youngest producer?

262
00:14:44,885 --> 00:14:47,754
- So Na, sit here.
- Okay.

263
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:11,478
Thanks for tonight.

264
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:13,981
Sorry.

265
00:15:14,181 --> 00:15:16,083
It's okay. Everyone's like that at first.

266
00:15:16,216 --> 00:15:17,184
Get home safely.

267
00:15:17,317 --> 00:15:18,585
I can't walk you out far.

268
00:15:19,052 --> 00:15:20,554
Okay, I'll see you.

269
00:15:21,054 --> 00:15:22,990
You'll get paid, so don't worry.

270
00:15:35,602 --> 00:15:37,671
When it rains, it pours.

271
00:15:50,918 --> 00:15:52,019
(Tak Mu I)

272
00:15:52,019 --> 00:15:53,687
Come out. Let's have coffee.

273
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:14,241
Didn't you say we'd have coffee?

274
00:16:14,608 --> 00:16:17,444
I thought this would be better
since you need to sleep.

275
00:16:17,945 --> 00:16:19,379
Thank you.

276
00:16:25,485 --> 00:16:26,486
Give it here.

277
00:16:29,656 --> 00:16:30,724
That was the wrong side.

278
00:16:43,504 --> 00:16:47,307
I never thought I'd drink milk this way.

279
00:16:48,709 --> 00:16:51,011
What way is that?

280
00:16:52,546 --> 00:16:54,448
On a rainy night,

281
00:16:54,648 --> 00:16:58,018
listening to one of my favorite songs
and looking out at the river.

282
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:02,089
- It has a certain charm, doesn't it?
- Yes.

283
00:17:02,155 --> 00:17:03,434
Even though it's near my home,

284
00:17:03,459 --> 00:17:05,993
I don't know how long it's been
since I came to the Han River.

285
00:17:07,261 --> 00:17:08,495
I come from time to time.

286
00:17:09,263 --> 00:17:10,264
You know what?

287
00:17:10,397 --> 00:17:13,767
I've heard celebrities often go on
secret dates around here.

288
00:17:17,871 --> 00:17:21,008
Well, I've heard many of them do.

289
00:17:22,709 --> 00:17:24,711
Like you've never done that before.

290
00:17:29,349 --> 00:17:32,186
I mean, it's happening right now.

291
00:18:07,487 --> 00:18:11,058
- The rain stopped.
- It did.

292
00:18:12,159 --> 00:18:15,229
Is it okay for you to be out here
during the shoot?

293
00:18:16,663 --> 00:18:19,099
Da Hong's solo scene is long,
so I got some time.

294
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:21,001
I see.

295
00:18:21,368 --> 00:18:25,105
But now that I've tried it myself,
I've realized acting is really hard.

296
00:18:25,839 --> 00:18:28,842
Shooting the same lines this way and that,
several times.

297
00:18:30,444 --> 00:18:32,779
Actors really are amazing.

298
00:18:33,614 --> 00:18:34,982
Writing is harder.

299
00:18:35,816 --> 00:18:37,618
I was thinking about it earlier.

300
00:18:37,885 --> 00:18:41,054
I'd love to act in something
Author Kkong wrote.

301
00:18:41,555 --> 00:18:44,291
- Just something I thought about.
- No way. That's absurd.

302
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:47,060
I've only ever written novels.

303
00:18:47,494 --> 00:18:49,263
What I felt while reading your book…

304
00:18:49,263 --> 00:18:51,999
was that it's a novel,
but I can picture every scene.

305
00:18:52,266 --> 00:18:53,667
I think your writing…

306
00:18:54,201 --> 00:18:55,202
How do I put it?

307
00:18:55,702 --> 00:18:58,939
I'd say somewhere between a novel
and a drama script.

308
00:19:04,511 --> 00:19:06,046
I don't write anymore.

309
00:19:10,117 --> 00:19:13,287
I wanted to ask why, but I didn't.

310
00:19:14,721 --> 00:19:16,290
Somehow, I felt the reason was...

311
00:19:16,924 --> 00:19:20,794
stuck in that time, somewhere
between the time she wants to go back to…

312
00:19:21,428 --> 00:19:26,300
and the time she doesn't want
to face again.

313
00:19:28,435 --> 00:19:30,170
By the way, about Da Hong.

314
00:19:30,571 --> 00:19:32,739
You said you'd known each other
as child actors.

315
00:19:34,074 --> 00:19:35,075
That's right.

316
00:19:35,375 --> 00:19:36,877
What was she like as a child?

317
00:19:36,877 --> 00:19:38,745
Was she bubbly back then too?

318
00:19:39,313 --> 00:19:43,016
For child actors, a set is
a pretty confusing place.

319
00:19:44,484 --> 00:19:48,121
Your TV mom would ask,
"Do you like your real mom or me?"

320
00:19:48,922 --> 00:19:52,259
If I didn't perform well, my guardian
would get scolded by the director,

321
00:19:52,759 --> 00:19:55,963
and during long waits, we did homework
and worked on study books.

322
00:19:57,664 --> 00:20:00,968
You can't tell if it's a school,
a workplace, or a playground.

323
00:20:01,602 --> 00:20:03,203
It was pretty complicated,

324
00:20:04,671 --> 00:20:07,774
but even then, Da Hong was so cheerful.

325
00:20:08,375 --> 00:20:11,178
I knew she was
a consummate professional even then…

326
00:20:14,815 --> 00:20:16,049
What? What's wrong?

327
00:20:21,088 --> 00:20:23,524
- Why are you hiding?
- You wouldn't understand.

328
00:20:26,627 --> 00:20:27,628
No, no, don't open it.

329
00:20:28,228 --> 00:20:30,230
I was never here, okay?

330
00:20:45,579 --> 00:20:47,281
What? Did you not see me?

331
00:20:47,481 --> 00:20:49,917
What are you doing here?
What about filming?

332
00:20:50,417 --> 00:20:53,520
It was canceled because of the sudden
rain, but it stopped quickly.

333
00:20:54,054 --> 00:20:55,989
Yeong Su said
he was going out for a drive.

334
00:20:56,323 --> 00:20:58,825
You used to come here to take breaks
for another shoot.

335
00:20:59,092 --> 00:21:00,727
Hey, what happened to your manager?

336
00:21:00,827 --> 00:21:02,262
I sent him off in a taxi.

337
00:21:02,462 --> 00:21:04,064
He was happy about leaving early.

338
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:10,838
Isn't that Yu Il?

339
00:21:11,705 --> 00:21:14,174
- What?
- Is she out for a walk?

340
00:21:15,075 --> 00:21:16,310
Yu Il!

341
00:21:17,244 --> 00:21:19,980
Hey, Yu Il!

342
00:21:28,288 --> 00:21:29,957
Hi, Da Hong!

343
00:21:31,558 --> 00:21:34,394
Yu Il! What brings you here?

344
00:21:38,365 --> 00:21:39,333
What?

345
00:21:41,935 --> 00:21:44,137
Well, why did you bring her here?

346
00:21:50,777 --> 00:21:51,985
Then what?

347
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:57,017
Then the chef showed up right then,
and told them,

348
00:21:58,719 --> 00:21:59,720
"I'm sorry."

349
00:22:00,153 --> 00:22:03,257
"I'd like to give you the wine
you were considering earlier."

350
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:05,125
"Would that be all right?"

351
00:22:05,659 --> 00:22:08,762
And then, look!

352
00:22:09,196 --> 00:22:10,284
It was over.

353
00:22:10,308 --> 00:22:11,565
Just like that.

354
00:22:12,466 --> 00:22:14,067
Chef Kang!

355
00:22:14,935 --> 00:22:16,136
How much was that wine?

356
00:22:16,470 --> 00:22:17,838
Turns out,

357
00:22:18,338 --> 00:22:20,474
it was over $700.

358
00:22:21,108 --> 00:22:22,075
$700?

359
00:22:22,643 --> 00:22:24,311
He won't take it out of your salary?

360
00:22:25,179 --> 00:22:26,747
No, no!

361
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:28,916
He's not that kind of person.

362
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:33,720
He said the staff's mistakes are
the owner's responsibility…

363
00:22:35,522 --> 00:22:36,790
It was so touching.

364
00:22:37,424 --> 00:22:39,593
- That's so cool.
- Very cool!

365
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:41,428
What's so cool?

366
00:22:41,495 --> 00:22:44,665
Anyway, I thought I'd get fired again.

367
00:22:47,434 --> 00:22:50,470
I want to be a full-time employee
somewhere too!

368
00:22:51,538 --> 00:22:54,341
Why can't I get a full-time job anywhere?

369
00:22:55,442 --> 00:22:58,011
- Should I pay for a shamanistic ritual?
- Yu Il!

370
00:22:58,579 --> 00:22:59,947
I'll read your tarot next time.

371
00:23:01,548 --> 00:23:03,016
You can read tarot too?

372
00:23:03,383 --> 00:23:06,353
Me? I'm totally amazing at it.

373
00:23:06,486 --> 00:23:08,785
- Right, Mu I?
- Yeah… sure.

374
00:23:09,990 --> 00:23:10,958
Yeah.

375
00:23:12,192 --> 00:23:14,595
I mean, job hunting is all fine and good,

376
00:23:14,595 --> 00:23:16,129
but would you consider writing again?

377
00:23:17,965 --> 00:23:18,966
No.

378
00:23:19,266 --> 00:23:20,868
I'm never writing again.

379
00:23:21,902 --> 00:23:24,404
I'm getting a real job,
like everyone else.

380
00:23:28,542 --> 00:23:29,910
Let me borrow this.

381
00:23:31,845 --> 00:23:32,813
Okay.

382
00:23:39,586 --> 00:23:40,687
She's very drunk.

383
00:23:41,555 --> 00:23:42,756
What are we going to do about her?

384
00:23:43,624 --> 00:23:44,691
Look!

385
00:23:46,627 --> 00:23:48,595
(Han River Convenience Store)

386
00:23:48,762 --> 00:23:49,730
Beep!

387
00:23:50,898 --> 00:23:51,932
Beep!

388
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:54,034
Beep!

389
00:23:55,569 --> 00:23:58,372
That'll be… $13.20.

390
00:23:58,672 --> 00:24:03,777
No, we're not at a convenience store.
This is an employee ID.

391
00:24:07,748 --> 00:24:08,949
Employee… ID…

392
00:24:09,316 --> 00:24:10,284
Employee ID.

393
00:24:10,417 --> 00:24:15,522
I want to tap my ID to walk into
the office like everyone else.

394
00:24:16,356 --> 00:24:18,759
And at lunchtime, I'd like to…

395
00:24:20,627 --> 00:24:22,196
drink some iced Americano.

396
00:24:24,398 --> 00:24:28,969
I'd also wear high heels
like a career woman.

397
00:24:29,336 --> 00:24:30,737
- She's so drunk.
- Careful.

398
00:24:31,405 --> 00:24:33,440
She wasn't this bad when she drank soju.

399
00:24:37,811 --> 00:24:38,979
Mu I! Your pants!

400
00:24:40,981 --> 00:24:43,684
- I'm so sorry!
- Don't touch him there! Come on!

401
00:24:44,451 --> 00:24:45,619
No, no, it's fine.

402
00:24:46,286 --> 00:24:47,487
I'm sorry.

403
00:24:49,323 --> 00:24:50,791
What do I do? I'm sorry.

404
00:24:51,725 --> 00:24:52,993
I'll go buy some wet wipes.

405
00:24:55,329 --> 00:24:57,931
- I'm sorry.
- You two, stay here.

406
00:24:57,931 --> 00:24:59,499
Yeah, Yeong Su, can you buy some?

407
00:24:59,499 --> 00:25:00,767
- Seriously.
- I'm so sorry.

408
00:25:04,238 --> 00:25:05,973
I knew something was off.

409
00:25:06,907 --> 00:25:07,941
What do you mean?

410
00:25:09,009 --> 00:25:10,277
I mean Mu I.

411
00:25:11,745 --> 00:25:14,348
He actually went to Yu Il's place
with a bouquet of flowers.

412
00:25:14,348 --> 00:25:15,582
I saw it for myself.

413
00:25:16,083 --> 00:25:17,551
- Flowers?
- Yeah.

414
00:25:18,051 --> 00:25:19,086
At the time,

415
00:25:19,319 --> 00:25:21,655
I heard Yu Il wrote his favorite book.

416
00:25:22,289 --> 00:25:25,592
So I let it go, but you saw it
earlier too, right?

417
00:25:26,159 --> 00:25:28,695
His pants got soaked,
but he only looked after Yu Il.

418
00:25:29,796 --> 00:25:32,766
Isn't that a little beyond basic manners?

419
00:25:32,833 --> 00:25:33,800
Come on.

420
00:25:34,301 --> 00:25:36,170
Because of him, she had hot coffee…

421
00:25:36,170 --> 00:25:38,939
splashed on her,
his absolute favorite author.

422
00:25:39,139 --> 00:25:42,176
So making a fuss over cold beer
wouldn't be right.

423
00:25:42,543 --> 00:25:46,079
- That's right. I forgot about that.
- Yeah.

424
00:25:46,079 --> 00:25:48,982
After the coffee incident, she lent him
that book to fulfill his dream.

425
00:25:48,982 --> 00:25:50,684
Of course he'd treat her like royalty.

426
00:25:50,684 --> 00:25:52,819
After all, he tried so hard
to find Kkong Kkong.

427
00:25:53,153 --> 00:25:55,856
And that book to Mu I is, how do I put it…

428
00:25:56,256 --> 00:25:59,359
Like a miracle drug?

429
00:26:00,394 --> 00:26:01,493
Anyway, that's how it is.

430
00:26:02,246 --> 00:26:03,330
It means that much?

431
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:07,201
When you become a fan late in the game,
you don't notice that you're up all night.

432
00:26:07,201 --> 00:26:08,468
It's the most exciting time.

433
00:26:09,536 --> 00:26:11,705
- Is that true?
- Yeah.

434
00:26:12,191 --> 00:26:13,207
Whatever.

435
00:26:13,974 --> 00:26:16,844
Something about Mu I keeps bothering me.

436
00:26:17,277 --> 00:26:19,379
Yu Il and fine dining…

437
00:26:21,515 --> 00:26:23,417
Was she with him at that fine dining date?

438
00:26:23,951 --> 00:26:24,985
No way.

439
00:26:32,559 --> 00:26:35,095
- What on earth is this?
- What is it?

440
00:26:35,095 --> 00:26:36,330
We're "family" now.

441
00:26:36,330 --> 00:26:37,598
Hang on, that's a contract.

442
00:26:37,965 --> 00:26:40,300
Hey, she signed with your company.

443
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:41,502
What?

444
00:26:42,169 --> 00:26:43,937
CEO Joo knows full well
about Min Ye and me.

445
00:26:44,805 --> 00:26:47,908
Sounds like something
your father would do.

446
00:26:48,041 --> 00:26:49,843
Dad, seriously.

447
00:26:50,577 --> 00:26:53,247
Call for a driver. Hurry! Get me a driver!

448
00:26:53,247 --> 00:26:54,248
Yeah, okay.

449
00:26:56,917 --> 00:26:58,385
I'll see you walk in before I go.

450
00:27:00,587 --> 00:27:04,658
You should never punch in your code
where anyone can see, got that?

451
00:27:06,193 --> 00:27:07,661
We're not looking.

452
00:27:07,961 --> 00:27:09,363
We'll turn around.

453
00:27:10,330 --> 00:27:12,266
You know, she seems sober enough.

454
00:27:12,266 --> 00:27:14,535
So no need to worry. Let's go.

455
00:27:15,435 --> 00:27:17,604
Sober! Right.

456
00:27:17,771 --> 00:27:18,872
Sober! Let's go.

457
00:27:18,872 --> 00:27:21,175
Thank you so much.

458
00:27:24,645 --> 00:27:27,080
- Hey, she's fine.
- Sober!

459
00:27:27,181 --> 00:27:29,650
- Hurry, go home.
- Okay, bye.

460
00:27:29,650 --> 00:27:30,918
- Bye.
- Okay, let's go.

461
00:27:36,657 --> 00:27:38,625
At first, I figured
since she's Author Kkong,

462
00:27:38,625 --> 00:27:40,694
it made sense to an extent.

463
00:27:41,695 --> 00:27:44,164
But no matter how I look at it,
it's just strange.

464
00:27:44,398 --> 00:27:46,300
Yeah, it is strange.

465
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:48,635
I'm always concerned about her.

466
00:27:48,869 --> 00:27:49,903
Hey.

467
00:27:51,305 --> 00:27:52,840
I'm asking just one thing of you.

468
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:55,742
Whatever you do, tell me first.

469
00:27:56,143 --> 00:27:59,012
That way, I can decide whether
to cover for you or not, okay?

470
00:28:04,284 --> 00:28:05,586
Hey, don't smirk like that!

471
00:28:06,186 --> 00:28:07,262
Seriously…

472
00:28:07,287 --> 00:28:08,288
I'm talking to you…

473
00:28:08,355 --> 00:28:10,824
(Central Library)

474
00:28:10,858 --> 00:28:13,927
(The Cover Letter That Gets You the Job)

475
00:28:22,803 --> 00:28:25,706
Beep! Beep! Beep!

476
00:28:29,176 --> 00:28:31,845
- I'm so sorry!
- Don't touch him there! Come on!

477
00:28:32,813 --> 00:28:34,982
I've lost my mind. I've lost it.

478
00:28:35,382 --> 00:28:38,018
How am I supposed to face him now?

479
00:28:41,855 --> 00:28:44,091
I have to give this back to him too.

480
00:28:57,804 --> 00:28:59,106
What's wrong with this?

481
00:29:00,207 --> 00:29:01,608
Where did my key card go?

482
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:08,115
I brought this with me by mistake.

483
00:29:09,783 --> 00:29:11,485
Mr. Tak Mu I!

484
00:29:12,252 --> 00:29:13,287
Mr. Tak…

485
00:29:17,191 --> 00:29:18,458
He's already gone.

486
00:29:28,669 --> 00:29:29,736
That hurts.

487
00:29:29,870 --> 00:29:32,406
Excuse me, do you have a boyfriend?

488
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:35,509
What? Who… who are you?

489
00:29:35,676 --> 00:29:37,044
I asked if you have a boyfriend.

490
00:29:38,912 --> 00:29:40,547
No, I don't.

491
00:29:41,481 --> 00:29:43,450
Then there's nothing between you two.

492
00:29:45,252 --> 00:29:47,221
You'd better keep it that way.

493
00:29:49,756 --> 00:29:50,757
Pardon?

494
00:29:53,093 --> 00:29:54,228
What was that?

495
00:29:55,810 --> 00:29:56,897
That hurts.

496
00:29:57,931 --> 00:30:00,834
No matter how hard I try,
I can't remember her face.

497
00:30:01,068 --> 00:30:02,736
It was definitely a woman.

498
00:30:05,339 --> 00:30:07,508
Could it be Song Yun O?

499
00:30:08,141 --> 00:30:10,811
(The Cover Letter That Gets You the Job)

500
00:30:11,912 --> 00:30:14,548
I'm sorry. My apologies.

501
00:30:28,562 --> 00:30:30,957
They've been talking for a long time.

502
00:30:30,981 --> 00:30:32,266
Who is it?

503
00:30:33,100 --> 00:30:35,936
A writer. A TV program writer.

504
00:30:36,236 --> 00:30:38,805
She keeps coming to ask him
to do a show together.

505
00:30:39,139 --> 00:30:41,341
My bro is so popular.

506
00:30:42,609 --> 00:30:45,445
There are a lot of cooking shows
these days.

507
00:30:45,913 --> 00:30:47,447
So he's not doing it?

508
00:30:47,781 --> 00:30:50,017
Our chef's family isn't exactly ordinary.

509
00:30:50,450 --> 00:30:52,986
I heard they're really wealthy.

510
00:30:53,420 --> 00:30:55,722
That family is quite strange.

511
00:30:56,123 --> 00:30:58,192
He achieved success
without any help from them.

512
00:30:58,192 --> 00:31:00,127
Yet they say,
"Don't do this. Don't do that."

513
00:31:01,328 --> 00:31:02,296
So bad.

514
00:31:04,898 --> 00:31:06,967
Okay, she's going. Let's go.

515
00:31:06,967 --> 00:31:07,969
Okay.

516
00:31:09,425 --> 00:31:10,581
Thanks for coming.

517
00:31:13,740 --> 00:31:14,808
Welcome in.

518
00:31:14,808 --> 00:31:16,677
- Let me show you to a table.
- Thanks.

519
00:31:21,281 --> 00:31:22,482
Thank you.

520
00:31:36,163 --> 00:31:38,332
Let's go somewhere else.

521
00:31:38,999 --> 00:31:40,033
What? Why?

522
00:31:40,901 --> 00:31:42,503
I suddenly want to eat something else.

523
00:31:42,503 --> 00:31:43,537
Why?

524
00:31:44,538 --> 00:31:45,939
The food is really good here.

525
00:31:45,939 --> 00:31:47,875
I want something spicy.

526
00:31:48,175 --> 00:31:49,443
- We'll come next time.
- Sorry.

527
00:31:49,443 --> 00:31:50,477
Okay.

528
00:31:51,411 --> 00:31:52,713
I'm telling you, it's good.

529
00:32:02,055 --> 00:32:04,358
(Gong Dong Hwan (5:00 PM))

530
00:32:23,944 --> 00:32:25,679
(Mom)

531
00:32:45,632 --> 00:32:47,401
Why did you show up without telling me?

532
00:32:47,434 --> 00:32:48,936
Well, you never answer my calls.

533
00:32:52,506 --> 00:32:53,941
Are you coming back from work?

534
00:32:55,142 --> 00:32:56,810
Why did you bother coming anyway?

535
00:32:57,978 --> 00:33:00,881
How many times have I said
I have something to say?

536
00:33:00,914 --> 00:33:02,282
Then say it.

537
00:33:07,187 --> 00:33:09,223
I told you, I'm okay with it.

538
00:33:09,223 --> 00:33:11,291
So are you going to keep doing this?

539
00:33:11,525 --> 00:33:13,927
How long will you hate your dad?

540
00:33:13,927 --> 00:33:16,263
How long will you go
without seeing your dad?

541
00:33:17,865 --> 00:33:20,300
Yu Il, your dad…

542
00:33:20,300 --> 00:33:21,668
Can you stop?

543
00:33:22,769 --> 00:33:23,937
I'm so tired right now.

544
00:33:24,071 --> 00:33:27,941
He got a job for you
at a company owned by a friend of his.

545
00:33:28,575 --> 00:33:31,945
You don't need to live
such a harsh life and struggle like this,

546
00:33:32,379 --> 00:33:33,680
when you have a supportive dad.

547
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,349
Mom, please stop!

548
00:33:35,749 --> 00:33:37,017
Just stop it!

549
00:33:37,084 --> 00:33:38,719
Today that man…

550
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:40,687
That man…

551
00:33:43,857 --> 00:33:45,425
What's the matter?

552
00:33:45,659 --> 00:33:47,594
What's wrong, Yu Il? What…

553
00:33:48,195 --> 00:33:49,663
Yu Il!

554
00:33:49,963 --> 00:33:51,064
Yu Il!

555
00:34:04,144 --> 00:34:05,712
You haven't gone home yet?

556
00:34:07,581 --> 00:34:08,682
Chef.

557
00:34:09,783 --> 00:34:10,817
Were you crying?

558
00:34:11,118 --> 00:34:12,619
Of course not.

559
00:34:13,253 --> 00:34:16,123
I was running to lose weight
and ended up here.

560
00:34:25,432 --> 00:34:27,968
Why are these onions so small?

561
00:34:28,502 --> 00:34:29,536
Cute, right?

562
00:34:30,003 --> 00:34:31,538
These are called shallots.

563
00:34:31,672 --> 00:34:33,340
If you pickle them,

564
00:34:33,607 --> 00:34:36,510
they taste milder than raw onions
and are rich in flavor too.

565
00:34:38,378 --> 00:34:39,580
So that's why.

566
00:34:40,013 --> 00:34:43,584
Now I see why customers at our place
ask for more pickles so often.

567
00:34:43,584 --> 00:34:44,751
I finally get it.

568
00:34:45,152 --> 00:34:48,822
Some customers tell me that they come
just for these addictive pickled shallots.

569
00:34:50,624 --> 00:34:51,692
Is it ours now?

570
00:34:52,659 --> 00:34:53,627
What?

571
00:34:54,228 --> 00:34:55,395
You said, "Our place."

572
00:34:58,298 --> 00:35:00,100
Of course it's "our place."

573
00:35:03,237 --> 00:35:04,271
Peel all of these.

574
00:35:05,038 --> 00:35:07,841
We're completely out of pickles,
so we have to make more.

575
00:35:08,041 --> 00:35:09,209
As for overtime pay,

576
00:35:09,209 --> 00:35:11,245
let's call it even with the spilled wine.

577
00:35:12,446 --> 00:35:14,948
Didn't you say that's just
the owner's responsibility?

578
00:35:15,949 --> 00:35:16,950
I take it back.

579
00:35:17,751 --> 00:35:19,219
Peel them all, quickly.

580
00:35:20,287 --> 00:35:22,256
You can go home once you finish these.

581
00:35:23,423 --> 00:35:25,192
Yes, understood, Chef.

582
00:35:31,565 --> 00:35:33,767
Let's go somewhere else.

583
00:35:34,568 --> 00:35:35,569
What? Why?

584
00:35:35,636 --> 00:35:37,704
I suddenly want to eat something else.

585
00:35:37,871 --> 00:35:40,107
How long will you hate your dad?

586
00:35:40,240 --> 00:35:42,876
How long will you go
without seeing your dad?

587
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:29,156
The tears just wouldn't stop.

588
00:36:30,324 --> 00:36:31,592
Thanks for doing that.

589
00:36:31,892 --> 00:36:35,162
Yu Il, do you have plans tomorrow?

590
00:36:35,762 --> 00:36:36,830
Not sure.

591
00:36:37,197 --> 00:36:38,732
It's a rare day off,

592
00:36:38,732 --> 00:36:40,868
so I was thinking of lounging around
at home.

593
00:36:41,802 --> 00:36:46,006
Tomorrow, I've been invited to attend the
premiere of the show "Rooftop Romance."

594
00:36:46,273 --> 00:36:47,274
Want to go with me?

595
00:36:48,642 --> 00:36:52,112
I heard about that from my friend
and Tak Mu I.

596
00:36:52,412 --> 00:36:53,614
But it's a VIP premiere.

597
00:36:53,947 --> 00:36:56,717
Since I'm no celebrity,
I think it'll be a bit awkward.

598
00:36:56,984 --> 00:36:59,119
So what? Let's go together.

599
00:37:00,621 --> 00:37:02,035
Aren't you curious…

600
00:37:02,102 --> 00:37:04,124
about how your rooftop place
may look on screen?

601
00:37:06,126 --> 00:37:07,661
Well, yes, but…

602
00:37:07,661 --> 00:37:10,330
It won't be just the two of us.
Kevin's coming too.

603
00:37:11,031 --> 00:37:13,433
That guy is a huge K-drama fan,

604
00:37:13,433 --> 00:37:15,502
and he's been begging for days.

605
00:37:15,936 --> 00:37:18,472
Seriously. I finally caved.

606
00:37:20,240 --> 00:37:22,209
So Kevin's going too.

607
00:37:22,643 --> 00:37:23,777
Yes.

608
00:37:23,911 --> 00:37:26,046
("Rooftop Romance")

609
00:37:32,085 --> 00:37:35,589
I guess you don't give flowers
to people here.

610
00:37:36,890 --> 00:37:39,960
- That's why they'll like it even more.
- You think so?

611
00:37:49,536 --> 00:37:50,904
This is your only chance…

612
00:37:50,904 --> 00:37:54,541
to catch "Rooftop Romance"
on the big screen.

613
00:37:54,741 --> 00:37:56,076
Thank you for joining us…

614
00:37:56,076 --> 00:37:59,112
for our premiere VIP screening.

615
00:37:59,580 --> 00:38:02,216
I'm your host, Producer Yoo Yeon Ju.

616
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:09,389
Introducing "Rooftop Romance"
tonight is...

617
00:38:09,389 --> 00:38:10,958
actor Tak Mu I.

618
00:38:17,364 --> 00:38:18,799
Our show "Rooftop Romance,"

619
00:38:18,799 --> 00:38:20,434
as the title suggests,

620
00:38:25,606 --> 00:38:27,074
Well, that is…

621
00:38:27,574 --> 00:38:30,043
It's a story that begins
in a rooftop room,

622
00:38:33,514 --> 00:38:34,781
Chef?

623
00:38:38,485 --> 00:38:41,955
It's a very sweet love story.

624
00:38:42,589 --> 00:38:45,212
It looks like Tak Mu I
is looking at you, Yu Il.

625
00:38:45,237 --> 00:38:46,293
Me?

626
00:38:46,994 --> 00:38:48,729
Come on, I bet he can't even see me.

627
00:38:48,729 --> 00:38:50,564
I'm too far away, and it's too dark.

628
00:38:50,797 --> 00:38:52,478
When someone is so…

629
00:38:53,643 --> 00:38:54,643
close…

630
00:38:55,469 --> 00:38:58,572
close beside you,

631
00:38:59,373 --> 00:39:02,409
you don't realize how precious
they are to you,

632
00:39:02,609 --> 00:39:06,180
then you realize it and get them back.

633
00:39:06,313 --> 00:39:07,714
What is he talking about?

634
00:39:07,714 --> 00:39:08,982
Was that about our show?

635
00:39:10,617 --> 00:39:14,054
Now that it's time to reveal
our show to everyone,

636
00:39:14,054 --> 00:39:15,189
I'm getting nervous.

637
00:39:15,322 --> 00:39:17,124
Please enjoy it. Thank you.

638
00:39:18,492 --> 00:39:20,427
He's a bit stiff today, isn't he?

639
00:39:21,161 --> 00:39:22,329
He is.

640
00:39:24,744 --> 00:39:28,378
Now, we present to you "Rooftop Romance."

641
00:39:28,445 --> 00:39:29,670
Please enjoy.

642
00:39:35,709 --> 00:39:36,748
Who are you?

643
00:39:37,845 --> 00:39:40,914
- A friend of the woman who lives here.
- A friend?

644
00:39:41,748 --> 00:39:43,784
And you are?

645
00:39:44,284 --> 00:39:46,053
I'm her younger brother.

646
00:39:46,386 --> 00:39:49,356
I'm sorry I wasn't
the one who invited you,

647
00:39:49,356 --> 00:39:50,691
but I hope you enjoy it.

648
00:39:51,892 --> 00:39:53,293
Wait, you say you're a friend,

649
00:39:53,293 --> 00:39:55,362
and you show up here unannounced?

650
00:39:55,996 --> 00:39:59,499
Or are you the kind of friend who can?

651
00:40:00,634 --> 00:40:02,870
Someone who wants to be that close.

652
00:40:07,348 --> 00:40:08,842
- This is so amazing.
- What?

653
00:40:09,810 --> 00:40:13,046
If I'd known you'd suffer so much
because of him,

654
00:40:13,547 --> 00:40:15,415
I'd have taken you from him long ago.

655
00:40:17,851 --> 00:40:19,486
People around me tell me…

656
00:40:20,354 --> 00:40:22,022
that the living must go on.

657
00:40:22,656 --> 00:40:23,957
But I…

658
00:40:26,426 --> 00:40:27,761
(Cast)

659
00:40:34,902 --> 00:40:36,837
I think now is the time
to give the flowers.

660
00:40:38,705 --> 00:40:40,574
I think I'll give these to them later.

661
00:40:40,707 --> 00:40:42,176
I feel too shy right now.

662
00:40:43,210 --> 00:40:44,611
Shall I do it for you?

663
00:40:44,811 --> 00:40:47,714
It airs starting this Friday at 10 PM.

664
00:40:47,714 --> 00:40:50,384
So please tune in.
We look forward to your support!

665
00:41:01,395 --> 00:41:02,896
What on earth are you doing?

666
00:41:14,274 --> 00:41:15,876
("Rooftop Romance" Premiere Bromance)

667
00:41:15,876 --> 00:41:17,611
(Mu I and Chef Kang, you should date!)

668
00:41:20,247 --> 00:41:21,982
I'm such a huge fan.

669
00:41:21,982 --> 00:41:23,984
You are so handsome!

670
00:41:29,923 --> 00:41:33,227
Hey, is it really okay for me to be here?

671
00:41:33,660 --> 00:41:38,098
Look, the chef is here, and his employee
is totally acting like a fan over there.

672
00:41:38,098 --> 00:41:39,533
But you made it on the show.

673
00:41:39,533 --> 00:41:41,568
Be proud. Shoulders back.

674
00:41:41,702 --> 00:41:43,270
Wait, you're on the show?

675
00:41:43,637 --> 00:41:45,472
Yes, she'll be in the arcade scene.

676
00:41:45,472 --> 00:41:47,474
- She gave a brilliant perfor…
- Hey!

677
00:41:47,474 --> 00:41:49,543
I told you to take it to the grave, right?

678
00:41:49,710 --> 00:41:50,844
Yes, ma'am.

679
00:41:52,946 --> 00:41:55,015
Kkong! Are you close with Tak Mu I?

680
00:41:55,349 --> 00:41:56,690
He asked if I worked with you,

681
00:41:56,757 --> 00:41:59,450
and when I said I did,
he took a photo with me.

682
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,521
Amazing! How do you two know each other?

683
00:42:01,588 --> 00:42:04,858
Well, I ended up lending him my house…

684
00:42:04,892 --> 00:42:06,827
Wait. Oh, my gosh.

685
00:42:06,827 --> 00:42:08,161
Then do you guys…

686
00:42:08,161 --> 00:42:10,074
- visit each other's houses…
- Kevin, stop.

687
00:42:11,434 --> 00:42:12,434
Yummy.

688
00:42:18,772 --> 00:42:19,873
Shall we have a drink?

689
00:42:19,873 --> 00:42:21,441
Did you go to the premiere?

690
00:42:21,441 --> 00:42:22,643
How did you know?

691
00:42:22,910 --> 00:42:23,977
(At a team dinner with the director)

692
00:42:23,977 --> 00:42:26,747
Traitor! You didn't even tell me.

693
00:42:26,747 --> 00:42:29,116
Sorry, it happened so suddenly.

694
00:42:35,389 --> 00:42:36,490
Ryu Min is there, right?

695
00:42:36,490 --> 00:42:39,159
Send me a photo of Ryu Min
and I'll forgive you!

696
00:42:39,259 --> 00:42:41,395
Great work, everyone. Cheers!

697
00:42:41,395 --> 00:42:42,362
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

698
00:42:42,362 --> 00:42:44,932
Thank you so much for working so hard.

699
00:42:45,065 --> 00:42:47,634
Fine, I'll take a photo with Ryu Min,

700
00:42:47,868 --> 00:42:50,003
return this, and then go home.

701
00:42:50,470 --> 00:42:52,072
Goodness, thank you so much.

702
00:42:55,676 --> 00:42:58,345
Director, I poured as much as I love you.

703
00:42:58,345 --> 00:43:00,147
That's too much love.

704
00:43:00,147 --> 00:43:01,515
I'm not into men, though.

705
00:43:01,582 --> 00:43:02,616
Cheers. Let's drink.

706
00:43:02,616 --> 00:43:04,051
- Cheers!
- Cheers, wait.

707
00:43:04,051 --> 00:43:05,018
Ryu Min's glass is empty.

708
00:43:05,018 --> 00:43:07,054
A drink for Ryu Min, cheers.

709
00:43:12,125 --> 00:43:13,293
Good work.

710
00:43:13,627 --> 00:43:16,029
- Yu Il, want to try some?
- Is it good?

711
00:43:18,532 --> 00:43:20,334
Director, I need to go to the restroom.

712
00:43:20,334 --> 00:43:22,269
- Wait.
- You do?

713
00:43:22,369 --> 00:43:23,704
Come back quickly.

714
00:43:24,004 --> 00:43:25,372
You have to take this drink.

715
00:43:25,372 --> 00:43:28,041
- You did a great job.
- You did a great job too.

716
00:43:29,510 --> 00:43:32,446
- I'll drink with you later.
- Hey, Mu I.

717
00:43:32,446 --> 00:43:33,413
(Feeling good)

718
00:43:33,413 --> 00:43:36,016
(Still fine)

719
00:43:36,016 --> 00:43:38,385
- Take a shot with us.
- Cheers!

720
00:43:39,052 --> 00:43:40,354
(Slightly drunk)

721
00:43:40,354 --> 00:43:42,189
Everyone, enjoy. Yeah.

722
00:43:44,758 --> 00:43:47,461
(A little more drunk)

723
00:43:47,461 --> 00:43:48,495
Mu I.

724
00:43:49,596 --> 00:43:51,031
- Good work.
- Cheers!

725
00:43:52,499 --> 00:43:57,671
(Drunk)

726
00:43:57,671 --> 00:43:59,139
(Dangerous)

727
00:44:02,809 --> 00:44:05,112
Yu Il, what did you think of the show?

728
00:44:05,445 --> 00:44:08,115
It was really fun.
I think it'll be a huge hit.

729
00:44:08,115 --> 00:44:09,116
Really?

730
00:44:09,116 --> 00:44:11,585
See, I do have an eye for scripts.

731
00:44:11,585 --> 00:44:13,520
Stay here with me until the end, okay?

732
00:44:13,520 --> 00:44:14,721
Okay.

733
00:44:20,227 --> 00:44:22,496
Hey, you lightweight.
You're already drunk?

734
00:44:23,030 --> 00:44:24,598
You can't hold your liquor.

735
00:44:26,667 --> 00:44:27,935
That's amazing.

736
00:44:27,968 --> 00:44:30,103
Did you tie your hair with your own hair?

737
00:44:30,404 --> 00:44:32,573
Hey! What are you saying?

738
00:44:32,940 --> 00:44:34,575
Where did your manager go?

739
00:44:35,209 --> 00:44:37,144
My head feels like it's splitting.

740
00:44:38,378 --> 00:44:41,515
Send me a photo of Ryu Min
and I'll forgive you!

741
00:44:58,465 --> 00:45:01,735
What do you, what do you,
what do you mean?

742
00:45:01,902 --> 00:45:02,870
Are you okay?

743
00:45:02,870 --> 00:45:05,839
What do you mean? Energy

744
00:45:13,747 --> 00:45:15,215
Where did everyone go?

745
00:45:26,727 --> 00:45:28,128
Have you eaten anything?

746
00:45:30,864 --> 00:45:31,999
Yes.

747
00:45:32,399 --> 00:45:33,867
Where were you earlier?

748
00:45:37,004 --> 00:45:38,605
I went to buy ice cream.

749
00:45:41,808 --> 00:45:43,810
Why did you buy so many?

750
00:45:43,810 --> 00:45:45,812
For everyone here to eat?

751
00:45:46,480 --> 00:45:47,481
No.

752
00:45:48,615 --> 00:45:51,552
I didn't know what you like, Kkong,

753
00:45:52,319 --> 00:45:54,254
so I just bought a bunch.

754
00:45:57,991 --> 00:45:59,593
I see.

755
00:45:59,593 --> 00:46:01,261
You didn't know what I like.

756
00:46:01,929 --> 00:46:03,931
I like this one.

757
00:46:13,240 --> 00:46:14,441
You know,

758
00:46:15,008 --> 00:46:17,077
I've been trying to come to this table.

759
00:46:18,846 --> 00:46:19,913
Why?

760
00:46:20,080 --> 00:46:21,615
Why do you think?

761
00:46:22,416 --> 00:46:24,084
Because of you, Author Kkong.

762
00:46:31,892 --> 00:46:34,094
The ice cream is sweet.

763
00:46:36,697 --> 00:46:37,707
By the way,

764
00:46:38,523 --> 00:46:39,525
I brought this.

765
00:46:40,067 --> 00:46:42,135
Sorry, was it inconvenient without it?

766
00:46:44,037 --> 00:46:45,205
Beep.

767
00:46:45,506 --> 00:46:46,540
Beep.

768
00:46:48,075 --> 00:46:49,977
You were really cute that night.

769
00:46:49,977 --> 00:46:53,347
My, you two look
very close over there.

770
00:46:54,414 --> 00:46:55,649
Excuse me for a moment.

771
00:46:55,816 --> 00:46:56,783
Who are you?

772
00:46:57,050 --> 00:46:58,118
Yes.

773
00:46:58,118 --> 00:47:02,256
I'm Park Hwi, a reporter from Yo Daily.

774
00:47:02,256 --> 00:47:03,690
Not "Bakwi," like cockroach.

775
00:47:03,690 --> 00:47:05,058
It's Park "Hwi."

776
00:47:05,058 --> 00:47:07,327
"Hwi."
I just wanted to be clear about that.

777
00:47:09,696 --> 00:47:13,934
The one who wrote the scandal piece
about Ryu Min and Da Hong?

778
00:47:14,268 --> 00:47:16,036
Well, yes, that's true.

779
00:47:16,036 --> 00:47:18,038
Everyone makes mistakes in life.

780
00:47:18,372 --> 00:47:19,873
But I was wondering,

781
00:47:19,940 --> 00:47:23,477
because I noticed earlier that this lady
seemed quite close to Mr. Tak Mu I.

782
00:47:23,577 --> 00:47:24,645
Who are you, I wonder?

783
00:47:42,629 --> 00:47:47,801
(Yo Daily News, Reporter Park Hwi)

784
00:47:51,305 --> 00:47:52,639
Hey, young lady with the bob.

785
00:47:53,640 --> 00:47:55,909
I asked what your relationship is
with Mr. Tak.

786
00:47:58,545 --> 00:47:59,947
I was crew.

787
00:48:01,114 --> 00:48:02,115
Crew?

788
00:48:03,350 --> 00:48:04,384
Wait a minute…

789
00:48:04,384 --> 00:48:06,153
Top star Tak Mu I personally buys,

790
00:48:06,153 --> 00:48:08,889
and gives ice cream to someone
who's only a crew member?

791
00:48:10,190 --> 00:48:12,860
What do you mean, only a crew member?

792
00:48:14,461 --> 00:48:15,929
So a crew member is...

793
00:48:15,929 --> 00:48:18,732
not allowed to be treated to ice cream
by a celebrity?

794
00:48:18,732 --> 00:48:20,367
Well, I don't see why not.

795
00:48:20,367 --> 00:48:23,403
But the celebrity in question is Tak Mu I.

796
00:48:23,670 --> 00:48:26,173
He's famous for keeping people
at arm's length.

797
00:48:26,740 --> 00:48:28,041
Tak Mu I.

798
00:48:30,677 --> 00:48:34,014
That sounds like it's aimed at me.

799
00:48:34,281 --> 00:48:37,851
Who told you that?
That I keep people at arm's length?

800
00:48:37,985 --> 00:48:39,653
Everyone says so. Everyone.

801
00:48:40,787 --> 00:48:41,855
Anyway,

802
00:48:41,855 --> 00:48:45,058
what kind of crew member are you,
young lady?

803
00:48:45,526 --> 00:48:47,594
Directing team? Or a stylist?

804
00:48:48,996 --> 00:48:50,264
It's really obvious, isn't it?

805
00:48:51,298 --> 00:48:54,201
That Tak Mu I is putting effort into her.

806
00:48:55,569 --> 00:48:56,837
Putting effort in?

807
00:48:57,104 --> 00:48:59,006
Is he making a move?

808
00:49:00,707 --> 00:49:02,876
She's working with me right now,

809
00:49:03,076 --> 00:49:06,446
and Mu I really wants her to work for him.

810
00:49:07,114 --> 00:49:10,417
She works very well, and she's diligent.

811
00:49:14,688 --> 00:49:16,356
You work well, and you're diligent?

812
00:49:16,690 --> 00:49:18,025
But here's the thing.

813
00:49:18,425 --> 00:49:21,728
Even though I love Tak Mu I so much,

814
00:49:24,464 --> 00:49:27,201
I can't give up such a capable talent.

815
00:49:28,135 --> 00:49:29,303
Hold on.

816
00:49:29,303 --> 00:49:31,138
You two… are in love?

817
00:49:31,405 --> 00:49:33,373
Yes. Also, I'm a fan of Tak Mu I.

818
00:49:34,141 --> 00:49:36,777
Forgive me. Where are my manners?

819
00:49:37,311 --> 00:49:38,812
I'm Chef Kang Hee Su.

820
00:49:39,947 --> 00:49:41,548
Yes, Kang Hee Su…

821
00:49:42,082 --> 00:49:44,918
The Michelin-starred chef
who studied abroad?

822
00:49:47,087 --> 00:49:49,489
Nice to meet you. I didn't recognize you.

823
00:49:49,489 --> 00:49:51,558
(Yo Daily News)

824
00:49:51,558 --> 00:49:54,228
Ta-da ta-da tan-ta-da ta-da ta-da

825
00:49:54,228 --> 00:49:55,229
Hey!

826
00:49:55,229 --> 00:49:57,798
Like you said, I worked the field
and landed a big story!

827
00:49:59,666 --> 00:50:01,935
I heard you went
to the "Rooftop Romance" premiere?

828
00:50:02,202 --> 00:50:03,470
Why did you even go to that?

829
00:50:03,670 --> 00:50:06,139
Weren't you embarrassed to see
Ryu Min and Joo Da Hong?

830
00:50:06,139 --> 00:50:07,741
Embarrassed, my foot.

831
00:50:07,741 --> 00:50:09,176
It happens.

832
00:50:09,476 --> 00:50:11,545
Hey, that's not the important part.

833
00:50:11,812 --> 00:50:13,514
I'm telling you, I landed a big one.

834
00:50:13,847 --> 00:50:14,882
What is it?

835
00:50:17,484 --> 00:50:18,752
It's a scoop, I tell you.

836
00:50:20,254 --> 00:50:21,288
Listen…

837
00:50:21,955 --> 00:50:25,025
So, you're saying that you, Chef Kang,

838
00:50:25,025 --> 00:50:27,694
were the man who gave Tak Mu I flowers.

839
00:50:28,729 --> 00:50:29,830
You saw that too.

840
00:50:29,830 --> 00:50:31,632
The female reporters outside...

841
00:50:31,632 --> 00:50:34,101
were going crazy, saying
you two look great together.

842
00:50:34,568 --> 00:50:37,704
These days, even between men,
they call it a bromance,

843
00:50:37,704 --> 00:50:39,873
and fans pair people up for fun.

844
00:50:40,340 --> 00:50:41,475
Well…

845
00:50:43,043 --> 00:50:44,178
that's what we wanted.

846
00:50:53,520 --> 00:50:54,588
Hello.

847
00:50:54,588 --> 00:50:57,057
Mu I, the director is looking for you.

848
00:50:58,058 --> 00:50:59,426
Let's go quickly.

849
00:51:10,504 --> 00:51:11,505
Let's have a drink.

850
00:51:19,179 --> 00:51:20,914
Tell me, Chef.

851
00:51:21,448 --> 00:51:23,984
Since when have you loved Tak Mu I…

852
00:51:23,984 --> 00:51:26,553
I mean, been a fan?

853
00:51:26,720 --> 00:51:29,489
Well, there's a lot to the story.

854
00:51:30,190 --> 00:51:33,289
- This is off the record.
- Yes?

855
00:51:34,394 --> 00:51:37,664
The truth is, because of our Mu I,

856
00:51:37,965 --> 00:51:40,834
I watched a drama show
for the first time ever.

857
00:51:43,036 --> 00:51:44,505
"Our Mu I?"

858
00:51:45,873 --> 00:51:49,376
This is an extremely personal reason,

859
00:51:51,111 --> 00:51:54,715
but I happened to catch a shower scene,

860
00:51:56,850 --> 00:51:58,752
which I found very sexy.

861
00:51:59,553 --> 00:52:01,188
I fell for him then…

862
00:52:02,523 --> 00:52:04,057
You found it sexy?

863
00:52:05,092 --> 00:52:06,827
Because I've lived overseas,

864
00:52:07,127 --> 00:52:09,897
I tend to be honest
in how I express my emotions,

865
00:52:09,897 --> 00:52:11,198
and direct about my feelings.

866
00:52:11,598 --> 00:52:15,636
This is what studying abroad does.
This is what you call open-mindedness.

867
00:52:16,670 --> 00:52:20,908
I've just realized that I've spilled
my secrets to a reporter, Mr. Park.

868
00:52:21,208 --> 00:52:24,144
I don't know if you'll remember all this.

869
00:52:24,745 --> 00:52:25,913
I'll remember.

870
00:52:27,447 --> 00:52:28,415
I'll remember.

871
00:52:28,882 --> 00:52:31,752
There was a reason Tak Mu I...

872
00:52:31,885 --> 00:52:35,756
never had a real scandal
even once until now.

873
00:52:37,324 --> 00:52:40,060
Something smells odd right now.

874
00:52:40,961 --> 00:52:42,129
Mr. Park.

875
00:52:45,465 --> 00:52:48,335
Mr. Park, that woman Tak Mu I
gave ice cream to,

876
00:52:48,335 --> 00:52:49,603
what does she look like?

877
00:52:51,471 --> 00:52:53,607
I keep telling you,
the woman isn't important.

878
00:52:53,607 --> 00:52:56,677
Exactly, since she's not important,
you can tell me.

879
00:52:56,677 --> 00:52:57,845
What does she look like?

880
00:52:58,378 --> 00:52:59,546
She's cute.

881
00:53:00,914 --> 00:53:02,749
She has a bob haircut. She's petite.

882
00:53:12,960 --> 00:53:16,830
But seriously, what if he actually writes
an article about what you said to him?

883
00:53:16,930 --> 00:53:19,766
I'd be happy to become famous.

884
00:53:20,801 --> 00:53:23,670
I thought you didn't like
the idea of fame.

885
00:53:23,670 --> 00:53:26,039
Really? You've misunderstood big-time.

886
00:53:28,509 --> 00:53:31,545
But you really hold your liquor well.

887
00:53:31,778 --> 00:53:34,715
I'm strong at everything.

888
00:53:40,020 --> 00:53:43,290
But that thing called curiosity…

889
00:53:44,491 --> 00:53:46,627
is such an interesting feeling.

890
00:53:47,995 --> 00:53:48,996
Sorry?

891
00:53:49,530 --> 00:53:51,398
I wonder if you've filled your stomach.

892
00:53:51,765 --> 00:53:53,467
Have you eaten anything?

893
00:53:54,635 --> 00:53:56,103
Where did everyone go?

894
00:53:56,937 --> 00:54:00,007
When they're out of sight,
you wonder where they went.

895
00:54:02,142 --> 00:54:04,411
I'm really curious about you too, Yu Il.

896
00:54:05,179 --> 00:54:07,381
About me? Why?

897
00:54:08,348 --> 00:54:09,449
I don't know.

898
00:54:10,083 --> 00:54:13,153
They say, "Know your enemy
and win a hundred battles."

899
00:54:14,855 --> 00:54:16,356
Am I the enemy?

900
00:54:17,591 --> 00:54:19,126
Not so much an enemy,

901
00:54:20,127 --> 00:54:23,363
as someone I want to get close to,
let's just say.

902
00:54:27,568 --> 00:54:31,438
Here comes someone who thinks
I'm the enemy.

903
00:54:35,642 --> 00:54:37,344
Why have you been out here so long?

904
00:54:38,779 --> 00:54:41,582
Well, you two talk, then.

905
00:54:56,930 --> 00:54:58,465
Finally, it's just the two of us.

906
00:54:59,900 --> 00:55:01,368
You drank a lot, didn't you?

907
00:55:02,503 --> 00:55:03,637
Thank you.

908
00:55:08,642 --> 00:55:10,611
- What are you doing here?
- You scared me!

909
00:55:11,512 --> 00:55:12,746
Have you sobered up a bit?

910
00:55:13,413 --> 00:55:14,581
What are you doing?

911
00:55:15,382 --> 00:55:17,317
Can't you tell? I'm spying on them.

912
00:55:17,651 --> 00:55:19,152
But why are you spying on them?

913
00:55:19,152 --> 00:55:21,388
Be quiet. I can't hear.

914
00:55:25,626 --> 00:55:26,994
But…

915
00:55:27,861 --> 00:55:29,596
Did you only buy this one?

916
00:55:31,565 --> 00:55:32,666
Or…

917
00:55:33,667 --> 00:55:35,569
Did you buy one for Chef Kang too?

918
00:55:39,373 --> 00:55:41,675
I did buy a few more…

919
00:55:43,110 --> 00:55:44,411
I don't like it.

920
00:55:47,848 --> 00:55:50,417
This is the most popular one, though…

921
00:55:50,884 --> 00:55:52,119
No.

922
00:55:52,853 --> 00:55:55,422
You working with Chef Kang,

923
00:55:56,390 --> 00:55:58,458
coming here together today,

924
00:55:58,992 --> 00:56:00,827
you guys even sitting side by side,

925
00:56:00,827 --> 00:56:02,829
I don't like any of it.

926
00:56:07,401 --> 00:56:10,437
I work with Chef Kang…

927
00:56:10,804 --> 00:56:12,539
because the hourly pay is good…

928
00:56:12,773 --> 00:56:16,109
and I'm free during the day, which gives
me time to prepare for interviews…

929
00:56:16,109 --> 00:56:17,511
Can't you just…

930
00:56:20,113 --> 00:56:24,051
Can't you just stay by my side?

931
00:56:27,354 --> 00:56:28,322
What?

932
00:56:41,201 --> 00:56:43,170
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
